A||||5||87FieroGTx||85 Fiero Won't start... help!!!||||5||
Z||000000||87FieroGTx||08-29-2001||12:23 AM|||| My 85 auto Fiero won't start!<P> A few days ago the batery died on me, Today I got it charged and the car started fine but about 20 miles later the car just died, but the raido still worked.<P> When I turn the key there is NOTHING!<P> But the radio lights and everything else works.<P> What Could it be?<P> A dead short?<P> Please I need help)||||reg||5
Z||000001||fierospeeder||08-29-2001||12:54 AM||||Your alternator might be bad.<P>Charge your battery up, and when its running, see what your volatage is in your dash.<P>14 while the car is running means its charging.  <P>12 while the car is running or not running means the battery isn't being charged.||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||08-29-2001||11:19 AM||||Yes it sounds like your alterntor is not chargeing the battery charge the battery up drive over to auto zone and they will check your chargeing system to see if you need a alternator.||||reg||1
Z||000003||87FieroGTx||08-29-2001||12:53 PM|||| So if the alternator is bad the starter won't turn?<P> Can the battery have enough power to run the radio and lights but not turn the starter?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Joe Torma||08-29-2001||01:00 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87FieroGTx:<BR>[BCan the battery have enough power to run the radio and lights but not turn the starter?[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes.  Also make sure you have good connections at the battery posts.  What happens to the headlights if you try to start the car with them on?  This can help pinpoint your prob.  How bright are the lights?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 08-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Leadfoot||08-29-2001||03:45 PM||||Check your connections.  Chances are you have a bad ground.  Get a set of jumper cables and connect one side to a nice clean spot on the engine and connect the other side on the neg post of the battery.  If that doesn't work you might not be getting juice to the starter or the starter solenoid is gone.  I would first clean all connections (this means jacking up the car to get to the starter).  I have had a similiar problem on my 85 (it was a bad ground) and another car I own did the same thing (solenoid was bad).  Do these simple tests before you dump over a hundred bucks into a battery and starter.....good luck!||||reg||1
